      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T11:22:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `ImportDexpreoptProperties` is the input to the `java_import` and `java_sdk_library_import`. Using it as the output for the sdk snapshot may seem like a good idea but it will cause problems in future. e.g. At the moment the whole structure is marked as being used from U+ but if an additional property is added to the structure in future release, e.g. V, then it will be necessary to annotate that property with something like `supported_build_releases:\"VeryNiceCake+\"` which will most likely cause problems with blueprint\u0027s handling of properties structures.\n\nI recommend that you simply add something like this here and in `sdk_library.go` instead:\n```\nDexPreoptProfileGuided *bool `supported_build_releases:\"UpsideDownCake+\"`\n```\n\nIf you want to share code between them then you can still use a structure but it would need to be different to `ImportDexpreoptProperties`.",
